{
  "id": 5,
  "title": "Editor Authoring — Drag, Edit, Reorder, Save",
  "goal": "Make the editor write-capable. Inspector inputs edit the in-memory scene and the canvas re-renders live. Drag from asset browser onto canvas adds a new layer at the drop position. Hierarchy supports drag-to-reorder and drag-into-group / drag-out-of-group. Save button persists the scene back to scenes/<id>/scene.json via a Vite middleware PUT endpoint. Loading picks up edits made externally (agent edits the same file on disk).",
  "prerequisites": [4],
  "status": "pending",
  "testing_strategy": "Manual: editor full authoring loop — drag the CODECAINE asset onto an empty scene, edit its position via inspector, reorder layers in hierarchy, save, reload page, confirm scene persists exactly. Edit scene.json on disk in another window, reload editor, confirm it reflects the external edit (proves agent-editability). Confirm save endpoint round-trips JSON without loss of properties or formatting differences that would break diffs.",
  "task_groups": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "Scene-mutation API + inspector inline editing",
      "objective": "Add the editor's authoring primitives (mutateLayerAt / addLayerAt / removeLayerAt / moveLayer + a dirty flag) to state.js, then convert the inspector's read-only <dl> into type-aware editable inputs that commit changes live so the canvas re-renders as the user types.",
      "status": "pending",
      "task_seeds": [
        { "title": "Add scene-mutation API + dirty flag to editor state", "intent": "Extend apps/scene-engine/editor/src/state.js with mutateLayerAt(path, patch), addLayerAt(parentPath, index, layer), removeLayerAt(path), moveLayer(fromPath, toPath), plus a dirty flag (markDirty/markClean/getDirty) and a 'dirty-changed' event. Mutators clone the scene shallowly along the path being changed (functional updates so canvas re-renderers see a new object), dispatch 'scene-changed' with the new scene and 'dirty-changed' with the new dirty flag. The shared path notation matches editor/src/path.js — '0', '0.children.2', etc. addLayerAt with parentPath '' targets the top-level layers array; non-empty parentPath targets layer.children. moveLayer is a remove + insert composed atomically (single scene-changed dispatch).", "processed": true, "task_id": 1 },
        { "title": "Inspector inline editing — type-aware inputs with live commit", "intent": "Refactor apps/scene-engine/editor/src/panels/inspector.js so dlPair becomes type-aware: numeric properties (opacity/scale/hue) render as <input type='number'> with appropriate step, blend renders as a <select> with css-blend-mode options, visible renders as <input type='checkbox'>, position.x/y and other strings as <input type='text'>. id/type/asset/layer remain read-only (re-keying those is structural — handled by reorder/drag flows). On input/change events, build a JSON Patch object reflecting the dotted key (e.g. 'properties.opacity' → { properties: { opacity: 0.5 } }) and call mutateLayerAt(currentPath, patch). Numeric inputs commit on 'input' (debounced 80ms); text inputs commit on 'change' (blur or Enter); checkbox/select commit on 'change'.", "processed": true, "task_id": 2 }
      ],
      "tasks": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "title": "Add scene-mutation API + dirty flag to editor state",
          "description": "Extend apps/scene-engine/editor/src/state.js with the editor's authoring primitives. (1) Add a `dirty` boolean to the store (default false) and a 'dirty-changed' event. Add markDirty(): if (!store.dirty) { store.dirty = true; bus.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('dirty-changed', { detail: true })); }. Add markClean(): if (store.dirty) { store.dirty = false; bus.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('dirty-changed', { detail: false })); }. Add getDirty(): return store.dirty. (2) Add helper splitPath(path): returns ['0','children','2'] style array; if path is '' return []. The dot/'.children.' encoding stays the same as editor/src/path.js — split('.children.') and re-join with .children. between segments. (3) Add helper cloneAlongPath(scene, segments): produces a new scene where every layer object on the path is shallow-copied (so the leaf can be mutated without touching siblings). Returns { scene: clonedScene, parent, indexInParent, layer } where parent is the array containing the leaf (top-level scene.layers or some children[]) and indexInParent is the leaf's index in that array. Implementation: recursively descend; at each level shallow-copy the array containing the next segment and the layer at that segment. (4) Add mutateLayerAt(path, patch): const segs = splitPath(path); if (segs.length === 0) return; const { scene, parent, indexInParent, layer } = cloneAlongPath(store.scene, segs); const merged = mergePatch(layer, patch); parent[indexInParent] = merged; store.scene = scene; markDirty(); bus.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('scene-changed', { detail: scene })). (5) Add helper mergePatch(target, patch): produces a new object with patch applied — for each key in patch, if patch[key] is a plain object AND target[key] is a plain object, recurse; otherwise patch[key] wins. Plain-object check: typeof === 'object' && !Array.isArray && constructor === Object. (6) Add addLayerAt(parentPath, index, layer): parentPath '' means top-level. Resolve parent via splitPath + cloneAlongPath (treating parentPath as a layer path that itself gets cloned + has its children array copied) — for parentPath '' the parent is scene.layers (clone scene + scene.layers). Splice layer in at index (clamped to [0, parent.length]). store.scene = newScene; markDirty(); dispatch 'scene-changed'. (7) Add removeLayerAt(path): splitPath; clone along path; parent.splice(indexInParent, 1); store.scene = newScene; clear selectedPath if it was equal-or-prefixed by the removed path; markDirty; dispatch. (8) Add moveLayer(fromPath, toPath): atomic — clone full scene once, perform an internal remove-by-path then insert-at-path on that single clone, then store.scene = newClone + single 'scene-changed' dispatch + markDirty. toPath is the target index path *as if the remove had not happened* — adjust the destination index by -1 if both paths share the same parent and toPath's last segment > fromPath's last segment (classic reorder index correction). For cross-parent moves no adjustment. (9) EXPORT mutateLayerAt, addLayerAt, removeLayerAt, moveLayer, markDirty, markClean, getDirty as named exports. Note: every mutator dispatches a single 'scene-changed' so canvas re-renders happen exactly once per logical edit. The dirty flag is set inside each mutator — callers don't need to also call markDirty.",
          "status": "pending",
          "context": {
            "read_before": [
              { "file": "apps/scene-engine/editor/src/state.js", "lines": "1-60", "purpose": "Locate existing store shape, bus dispatching, and getState/subscribe API — new mutators extend this without touching established setters" },
              { "file": "apps/scene-engine/editor/src/path.js", "lines": "1-40", "purpose": "Path encoding contract that splitPath must mirror exactly so mutateLayerAt, addLayerAt, removeLayerAt accept the same path strings the hierarchy/inspector already produce" },
              { "file": "apps/scene-engine/scenes/title/scene.json", "lines": "1-60", "purpose": "Reference scene shapes — confirms cloneAlongPath needs to handle nested children (codecaine-logo.children) and that layer objects mix flat keys (id/type/asset) with nested ones (position, properties)" }
            ],
            "related_files": [
              "apps/scene-engine/editor/src/panels/inspector.js",
              "apps/scene-engine/editor/src/panels/canvas.js"
            ]
          },
          "depends_on": [],
          "file_context": {
            "beginning": {
              "files": [
                { "path": "apps/scene-engine/editor/src/state.js", "status": "exists", "description": "From CP4 task 2: pub/sub store with setScene/setRegistry/setSelectedPath/subscribe/getState; no mutators or dirty flag yet" }
              ],
              "tree": null
            },
            "ending": {
              "files": [
                { "path": "apps/scene-engine/editor/src/state.js", "status": "modified", "description": "Adds dirty flag + mutateLayerAt + addLayerAt + removeLayerAt + moveLayer + markDirty/markClean/getDirty; functional clone-along-path; single scene-changed dispatch per mutator" }
              ],
              "tree": null
            }
          },
          "actions": [
            { "id": 1, "command": "UPDATE apps/scene-engine/editor/src/state.js: ADD `dirty: false` field to the existing `store` object literal alongside scene/registry/selectedPath", "file": "apps/scene-engine/editor/src/state.js", "status": "pending" },
            { "id": 2, "command": "ADD FUNCTION markDirty(): if (!store.dirty) { store.dirty = true; bus.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('dirty-changed', { detail: true })); }", "file": "apps/scene-engine/editor/src/state.js", "status": "pending" },
            { "id": 3, "command": "ADD FUNCTION markClean(): if (store.dirty) { store.dirty = false; bus.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('dirty-changed', { detail: false })); }", "file": "apps/scene-engine/editor/src/state.js", "status": "pending" },
            { "id": 4, "command": "ADD FUNCTION getDirty(): return store.dirty", "file": "apps/scene-engine/editor/src/state.js", "status": "pending" },
            { "id": 5, "command": "UPDATE setScene to also call markClean() after dispatching 'scene-changed' so freshly-loaded scenes start clean (loader.js calls setScene right after fetching from disk; an external reload should not appear dirty)", "file": "apps/scene-engine/editor/src/state.js", "status": "pending" },
            { "id": 6, "command": "ADD FUNCTION isPlainObject(v): return v !== null && typeof v === 'object' && !Array.isArray(v) && (v.constructor === Object || v.constructor === undefined)", "file": "apps/scene-engine/editor/src/state.js", "status": "pending" },
            { "id": 7, "command": "ADD FUNCTION mergePatch(target, patch): const out = { ...target }; for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(patch)) { if (isPlainObject(v) && isPlainObject(target?.[k])) out[k] = mergePatch(target[k], v); else out[k] = v; } return out", "file": "apps/scene-engine/editor/src/state.js", "status": "pending" },
            { "id": 8, "command": "ADD FUNCTION splitPath(path): if (!path) return []; return path.split('.children.')", "file": "apps/scene-engine/editor/src/state.js", "status": "pending" },
            { "id": 9, "command": "ADD FUNCTION cloneAlongPath(scene, segs): if (segs.length === 0) return { scene: { ...scene, layers: [...scene.layers] }, parent: null, indexInParent: -1, layer: null }; const sceneClone = { ...scene, layers: [...scene.layers] }; let parentArr = sceneClone.layers; let layer = parentArr[Number(segs[0])]; if (!layer) return null; layer = { ...layer }; parentArr[Number(segs[0])] = layer; for (let i = 1; i < segs.length; i++) { if (!Array.isArray(layer.children)) return null; layer.children = [...layer.children]; const idx = Number(segs[i]); const next = layer.children[idx]; if (!next) return null; const nextClone = { ...next }; layer.children[idx] = nextClone; parentArr = layer.children; layer = nextClone; } const indexInParent = Number(segs[segs.length - 1]); return { scene: sceneClone, parent: parentArr, indexInParent, layer }", "file": "apps/scene-engine/editor/src/state.js", "status": "pending" },
            { "id": 10, "command": "ADD FUNCTION mutateLayerAt(path, patch): if (!store.scene) return; const segs = splitPath(path); if (segs.length === 0) return; const result = cloneAlongPath(store.scene, segs); if (!result) return; const merged = mergePatch(result.layer, patch); result.parent[result.indexInParent] = merged; store.scene = result.scene; markDirty(); bus.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('scene-changed', { detail: result.scene }))", "file": "apps/scene-engine/editor/src/state.js", "status": "pending" },
            { "id": 11, "command": "ADD FUNCTION addLayerAt(parentPath, index, layer): if (!store.scene) return; const sceneClone = { ...store.scene, layers: [...store.scene.layers] }; let parentArr; if (!parentPath) { parentArr = sceneClone.layers; } else { const segs = splitPath(parentPath); const result = cloneAlongPath(sceneClone, segs); if (!result) return; result.parent[result.indexInParent].children = Array.isArray(result.layer.children) ? [...result.layer.children] : []; parentArr = result.parent[result.indexInParent].children; } const i = Math.max(0, Math.min(parentArr.length, index)); parentArr.splice(i, 0, layer); store.scene = sceneClone; markDirty(); bus.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('scene-changed', { detail: sceneClone }))", "file": "apps/scene-engine/editor/src/state.js", "status": "pending" },
            { "id": 12, "command": "ADD FUNCTION removeLayerAt(path): if (!store.scene) return; const segs = splitPath(path); if (segs.length === 0) return; const result = cloneAlongPath(store.scene, segs); if (!result) return; result.parent.splice(result.indexInParent, 1); store.scene = result.scene; if (store.selectedPath && (store.selectedPath === path || store.selectedPath.startsWith(path + '.children.'))) { store.selectedPath = null; bus.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('selection-changed', { detail: null })); } markDirty(); bus.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('scene-changed', { detail: result.scene }))", "file": "apps/scene-engine/editor/src/state.js", "status": "pending" },
            { "id": 13, "command": "ADD FUNCTION moveLayer(fromPath, toPath): if (!store.scene || !fromPath || !toPath || fromPath === toPath) return; const fromSegs = splitPath(fromPath); const toSegs = splitPath(toPath); if (fromSegs.length === 0 || toSegs.length === 0) return; const fromParentSegs = fromSegs.slice(0, -1); const toParentSegs = toSegs.slice(0, -1); const fromIdx = Number(fromSegs[fromSegs.length - 1]); let toIdx = Number(toSegs[toSegs.length - 1]); const sameParent = fromParentSegs.length === toParentSegs.length && fromParentSegs.every((s, i) => s === toParentSegs[i]); if (sameParent && toIdx > fromIdx) toIdx -= 1; const removeRes = cloneAlongPath(store.scene, fromSegs); if (!removeRes) return; const moved = removeRes.layer; removeRes.parent.splice(removeRes.indexInParent, 1); let parentArr; if (toParentSegs.length === 0) { parentArr = removeRes.scene.layers; } else { const insertRes = cloneAlongPath(removeRes.scene, toParentSegs); if (!insertRes) return; insertRes.parent[insertRes.indexInParent].children = Array.isArray(insertRes.layer.children) ? [...insertRes.layer.children] : []; parentArr = insertRes.parent[insertRes.indexInParent].children; } parentArr.splice(Math.max(0, Math.min(parentArr.length, toIdx)), 0, moved); store.scene = removeRes.scene; markDirty(); bus.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('scene-changed', { detail: removeRes.scene }))", "file": "apps/scene-engine/editor/src/state.js", "status": "pending" },
            { "id": 14, "command": "EXPORT mutateLayerAt, addLayerAt, removeLayerAt, moveLayer, markDirty, markClean, getDirty as named exports — extending the existing export list", "file": "apps/scene-engine/editor/src/state.js", "status": "pending" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "title": "Inspector inline editing — type-aware inputs with live commit",
          "description": "Refactor apps/scene-engine/editor/src/panels/inspector.js so the read-only <dl> becomes editable. Keep id/type/asset/layer as read-only text (those are structural — re-keying handled by drag/move flows in CP5 task 3+4). Make every other property an appropriate input type that commits via mutateLayerAt: (1) Add fieldFor(key, value, currentPath) → returns a DOM element appropriate to the value's semantics. Rules: key 'visible' (when present, value boolean) → <input type='checkbox' checked={value}> committing on 'change' with patch { visible: e.target.checked }; key matches /^properties\\.(opacity|scale|hue)$/ AND value is number → <input type='number' step={key.endsWith('opacity')||key.endsWith('scale')?'0.01':'1'} min={key.endsWith('opacity')?'0':undefined} max={key.endsWith('opacity')?'1':undefined} value={value}> committing debounced 80ms on 'input' with nested patch (e.g. { properties: { opacity: Number(e.target.value) } }); key matches /^properties\\.blend$/ → <select> with options ['normal','multiply','screen','overlay','darken','lighten','color-dodge','color-burn','hard-light','soft-light','difference','exclusion','hue','saturation','color','luminosity'] selected={value}, committing on 'change' with { properties: { blend: e.target.value } }; key matches /^position\\.(x|y)$/ → <input type='text'> (string-or-number; 'center', '33%', or '720'); commits on 'change' with { position: { x: parsed } } where parsed = Number(value) if /^-?\\d+(\\.\\d+)?$/ else raw string; default: <input type='text'> with the property merged the obvious way. (2) Replace dlPair with editorPair(dl, key, value, currentPath, readOnly = false): const dt = ...; const dd = ...; if readOnly OR value === undefined OR value === null create a <span> with String(value??''); otherwise dd.appendChild(fieldFor(key, value, currentPath)). (3) Build a small patchFromKey(key, value) helper that turns 'properties.opacity' + 0.5 into { properties: { opacity: 0.5 } } using key.split('.') reduce-into-nested-object. (4) Update renderLayerDl(layer, currentPath): id/type/asset/layer pairs use editorPair(..., readOnly=true); visible (only if defined) uses editorPair(..., readOnly=false); position.x / position.y editable when present; every key in layer.properties gets editorPair('properties.'+k, v, currentPath, false). (5) renderInspector now passes selectedPath as currentPath through to renderLayerDl. (6) Add module-scope debouncer: const debounceMap = new WeakMap(); debounce(el, fn, ms) — clears prior timer keyed by el, sets new. (7) IMPORTANT: each input change calls mutateLayerAt(currentPath, patch); state.js dispatches scene-changed which triggers renderInspector again — to prevent the user's focused input from being torn down on every keystroke, renderInspector must skip a full replaceChildren when (a) the current selectedPath matches the rendered path AND (b) document.activeElement is inside the panel — instead, only the canvas re-renders. Implementation: track lastRenderedPath in module scope; if equal AND focusedFieldKey is known, return early after refreshing only the non-focused fields' values via querySelectorAll('[data-key]') updates. Simplest correct cut: renderInspector compares (selectedPath, scene-version) — re-render fully only when selectedPath changes; on scene-changed alone, walk existing field DOM and update value attribute (and select-selected) by re-resolving layer + key via data-key attributes. Add data-key={key} to each input so this lookup is O(n) over visible fields. (8) APPEND CSS to editor.css: .inspector-list input[type='text'], .inspector-list input[type='number'], .inspector-list select { background:#0f0f0f; color:#ddd; border:1px solid #333; padding:2px 4px; font: inherit; min-width:0; width:100% } ; .inspector-list input[type='checkbox'] { accent-color:#4d8 }. After this task: clicking a CODECAINE sub-layer in hierarchy → inspector shows id/type/asset as text + opacity/hue as number inputs + visible as checkbox; tweaking opacity slider/spin updates the live canvas within ~80ms; the focused input does not lose focus across the resulting scene-changed dispatch.",
