              "title": "Vite save plugin — PUT /api/scenes/:id middleware",
              "description": "Add a small Vite dev-server plugin that handles persistence. (1) UPDATE apps/scene-engine/vite.config.js: ADD imports at top — `import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url'`, `import path from 'node:path'`, `import fs from 'node:fs/promises'`. (2) ADD FUNCTION sceneSavePlugin() at module scope BEFORE defineConfig — returns a Vite plugin object: { name: 'scene-engine:save', configureServer(server) { server.middlewares.use('/api/scenes/', async (req, res, next) => { try { const idMatch = req.url.match(/^\\/([\\w-]+)\\/?(?:\\?.*)?$/); if (!idMatch) { res.statusCode = 404; res.end('not found'); return; } const sceneId = idMatch[1]; if (!/^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$/.test(sceneId)) { res.statusCode = 400; res.end('invalid scene id'); return; } if (req.method !== 'PUT') { res.statusCode = 405; res.setHeader('Allow', 'PUT'); res.end('method not allowed'); return; } const chunks = []; for await (const chunk of req) chunks.push(chunk); let body; try { body = JSON.parse(Buffer.concat(chunks).toString('utf8')); } catch (err) { res.statusCode = 400; res.end('invalid json'); return; } if (!body || typeof body !== 'object' || Array.isArray(body)) { res.statusCode = 400; res.end('body must be a json object'); return; } const __dirname = path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)); const scenePath = path.resolve(__dirname, 'scenes', sceneId, 'scene.json'); const sceneDir = path.dirname(scenePath); await fs.mkdir(sceneDir, { recursive: true }); await fs.writeFile(scenePath, JSON.stringify(body, null, 2) + '\\n', 'utf8'); res.statusCode = 204; res.end(); } catch (err) { console.error('[scene-engine:save] error', err); res.statusCode = 500; res.end('internal error'); } }); } }. (3) UPDATE the existing defineConfig export — add plugins: [sceneSavePlugin()] (creating the plugins array if not present). (4) NOTE: the regex allows kebab-case like 'title' or 'main-menu' but rejects path-traversal ('..', '/', or absolute paths). The path.resolve under __dirname + 'scenes' is the second guard — if a sceneId somehow leaks dots/slashes path.resolve would still keep it inside scenes/<id>/, but the regex makes that impossible. (5) Confirm the middleware path matches Vite's middlewares.use('/api/scenes/', handler) which strips that prefix from req.url; req.url starts with '/<id>...' inside the handler. Sanity test: PUT /api/scenes/title with body { id:'title', layers:[] } → 204 → file at apps/scene-engine/scenes/title/scene.json overwritten with that JSON pretty-printed. PUT /api/scenes/../etc/passwd → middleware never matches because the regex rejects '..'. After this task, with `npm --prefix apps/scene-engine run dev` running, `curl -X PUT http://localhost:5173/api/scenes/title -H 'content-type: application/json' -d @apps/scene-engine/scenes/title/scene.json` returns 204 and the file's mtime updates without content drift.",
